[{"id":"VRCE-3-58-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":1,"english":"As Rāma went on, his feet failed him, his left eye to beat, and a trembling came over his frame.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a16be8f8329075fc25a3a67a1373a386cdefb6d88207b6e4377a86d4e5d84965","compact":"199f7d489fe4c1d6f3840fd0d69b6d063cd22ccfd757ea3ff65310d972b3334e","nasal":"92feecd468c1d1837f316483f77ff4373316415c229faf536aef8a528417fc86"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":2,"english":"Seeing again and again all these signs, he continually kept on asking (Lakşmaņa), Is it well with Sita?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4fcda9b376cd3a219558baa725c6905f5c8498d0888a1c30091a0e2c737e552e","compact":"798d09b6aa6ed0078ada94661d8b1d95a57af4e44e5d27c9e7d09bf5f57d3155","nasal":"798d09b6aa6ed0078ada94661d8b1d95a57af4e44e5d27c9e7d09bf5f57d3155"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":3,"english":"Eager to behold Sītā, he proceeded fast; but finding the abode empty, he was filled with anxiety.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c77c24ed1d38ce73b96a89ea0f2089e51fe2dbdd0301978b9fed4d4a923391a3","compact":"24d0d56ccdc77bf752b9798361271c3e1bcae6e15d8af54916034c83cf42bd44","nasal":"24d0d56ccdc77bf752b9798361271c3e1bcae6e15d8af54916034c83cf42bd44"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":4,"english":"And proceeding with swiftness, throwing about his limbs, Raghu's son began to survey all around the hut. He then found it empty of Sītā, like to a tank in evil plight and bereft of lotuses-during the winter.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e9424c2f3f856e26f7f12b92a4ac4bedb8e72ea7ac4b33187a15ecf3becad8fa","compact":"b37836172a42875062e63f6490d57999883055515409b8c91986eeee72854e68","nasal":"1b795faf43b81bc530ea11c47cfecfa58ebe457388478b9fa7383dd3d8c205a3"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":5,"english":"And proceeding with swiftness, throwing about his limbs, Raghu's son began to survey all around the hut. He then found it empty of Sītā, like to a tank in evil plight and bereft of lotuses-during the winter.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.705,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5dd54ef12e226b7cea5c62454bd5f65d608cf2e800630e2537ab9e76e4afad83","compact":"60ee2bae36631f9469c5fdffcfe589f887137c86570768e726f1ad99565db122","nasal":"7727fc0e1f29568a2cf9b84be210d1a9478e929f63105d872b5491b577273a10"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":6,"english":"And seeing the cottage empty, with its trees as if sorrowing, and its flowers faded, and its beasts and birds sunk in gloom, shorn of grace, worn out, forsaken by the sylvan deities, strewn with deer-skins and Kusa, and twists of Kasa, he wept again and again.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.765,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b89189fb31a0884c22807f1279980caafb25da3cb4cd3fac67f49e2913c574de","compact":"10a62dc02c768d6e94a429eeea6dd743ee3ffaadab2f599b0b89b0b7a8d955e1","nasal":"fd7a269d95b2e783236e6da2d67c192c17228a43c109184cb4a6907b2953bd64"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":7,"english":"And seeing the cottage empty, with its trees as if sorrowing, and its flowers faded, and its beasts and birds sunk in gloom, shorn of grace, worn out, forsaken by the sylvan deities, strewn with deer-skins and Kusa, and twists of Kasa, he wept again and again.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6fdfc0f4ce812388e7746f4602f21be999aa7dd44d98e07753592dc6616315f3","compact":"e53d76c9daa9b8958bd95ba4361fe0152b14803a392d4cff33dee28876c7e788","nasal":"e53d76c9daa9b8958bd95ba4361fe0152b14803a392d4cff33dee28876c7e788"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":8,"english":"Has the timid one been carried off, or is she dead, or has any one eaten her up, or has she vanished (from the earth), or has she gone to the wood, or has she gone to cull flowers and fruits, or has she gone to the pool for procuring water, or has she repaired to the river?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ea9bffab3576eb5d58d65efb94bda8f98cc26f5f6a2241514bdafb8f0ca96493","compact":"89042b092be4e08a2af63bff92369c6896c8b83d1edc7a672c4238bbe06856cc","nasal":"8