confidence":0.381,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c7fc80ceceb37b53217855b132b89dece2527424d85af76eadb3f797b9d4c72","compact":"9fc2c1663a471ef47d56d605c3176baba0a76d1aa74b7ef7a6d2cd347f19312f","nasal":"ceedab6d301070526f8d5236fa97fb0930a08a00b804e8c9bca53b45cf05d235"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":20,"english":"Again addressed he the diverse animals-O dear, know you for certain about Janakī having the eyes of a doe; is she engaged in play with the does?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058020","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1cd9465201520c7149452689f66a71a393f26f0ac3a7deb973e943b09f5dd461","compact":"9a42a4a86937dab75965c49be6abbcfb2455e2e24bdd87db436e45757268dd6a","nasal":"e808fc43149b7a69b29ff3c3f5f8869df79983944955fe26b9bb5a12e66e6ed4"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-21","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":21,"english":"O elephant, methinks you do know about the daughter of Janaka having thighs resembling your trunk; pray tell me if you have beheld her.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.7,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058021","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b7aaab062d555efb7bc913071163b67fd32e4659030b8bba065befd3555298b7","compact":"0d3caf4a6b62f1c5bfa330ef9c0e31996970e84bdd016bae27f4256f84639fff","nasal":"0d3caf4a6b62f1c5bfa330ef9c0e31996970e84bdd016bae27f4256f84639fff"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-22","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":22,"english":"O tiger, fearlessly do you relate to me if you have seen my beloved Maithilī, having a countenance resembling Moon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.883,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058022","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2b9183ceb03bab675a9d7c5cd5d2af929cff1a37382e8bbc3e6894eebcff0973","compact":"60efbaecb1b8ccec41cb6b6fed73aae89e254dafe4ba703d0e3f3f9e7c92f499","nasal":"7430272258961beba6b7d2dbabbe2f81dad63dd8fa9a8255359f16c2d96da4be"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-23","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":23,"english":"O dear! O you having eyes like to lotuses! why do you fly away? Surely have I seen you. Why do you not address me hiding yourself behind the tree?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058023","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5d48c499685f1a01510f75fd8431b392bc4078ea3c406e89fd829f12882f8433","compact":"47ce1b1e1d6c04731cec3ea3f30d8ee85318da7dfeb774733e3ee00cc88e939a","nasal":"47ce1b1e1d6c04731cec3ea3f30d8ee85318da7dfeb774733e3ee00cc88e939a"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-24","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":24,"english":"Wait, wait, O you fair damsel, you have no compassion for me! Never had you mock me before in this way! Why do you neglect me now?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058024","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2645fbbdedc43ecbd532667564e432448bdc352ec01a50a1b84d75dfe2e39d0d","compact":"b044bd244c7c8a80353db1d41f782d5af28be823b18384c538ba370be5215143","nasal":"b044bd244c7c8a80353db1d41f782d5af28be823b18384c538ba370be5215143"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-25","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":25,"english":"O exquisitely fair damsel, truly have I found you out from this your yellow silken cloth. I have seen you flying away. Stand if you have any love for me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.885,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058025","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"60d17cb7c61a9644b31eafc97fc0f76a942fe3eea5e852347dc65e98ae513187","compact":"367cf1325fa7929eb5bbc52058fd3f6ce7c259ff901b182dee6c522bd46961bb","nasal":"dfa3994a3c696dfb019fe14f18bd02bacfbe7991305523f91772d527e36d56ad"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-26","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":26,"english":"Or, O you having a sweet smile, you are not she; truly you have been killed or else you would not have neglected me at this time of dire affliction.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058026","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c80196ef74b2e954bf6c64d29b9746d265b5106c53144550d7c13eca8141163b","compact":"d2f2cb423718f709bb153fd088f0d0bac67a3f6813c070256ba6e6d5ff634e74","nasal":"d2f2cb423718f709bb153fd088f0d0bac67a3f6813c070256ba6e6d5ff634e74"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-27","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":27,"english":"True it is that she has been devoured in my absence by the Rākşasas living on flesh having torn into pieces her limbs.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058027","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e17f3ff1eddd98b66eebd7d2326669f9bee77dd5ee430fcdda983708060ab564","compact":"c063e502cbfaf5db799aacecde52b52c0eedfeec023d2df7a0445ed9ea5ce611","nasal":"35d9ce45fbd1e903acef9fd1d4fcddcc5c14dac2052ae38813f219bedaefaa58"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-28","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":28,"english":"Truly has her face, resembling the full-moon, having beautiful teeth a fine nose and white Kundalas, become of pale countenance being brought under the possession of the Rākșasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.303,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058028","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ced288393e5ce63a9980f169385cb12954e0e6267baa3b542d022b9dd2dbb820","compact":"a6d44fe3978741afe08d6b63faf5056637b418ab6039d9e722160b136a9404ca","nasal":"49b2c3a093ac6269f1e7204fd2c9d9421ae24261524029d6fb5ecfb717135996"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-29","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":29,"english":"Her neck had the hue of sandal and was adorned with necklace—that beautiful tender neck was eaten up by the Rākşasas, my beloved wife wailing. Her arms were tender like leaves and adorned with various ornaments; truly have the Rākşasas eaten them up, shaken as they were, by throwing them here and there.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.484,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-26","DUTT-3-60-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058029","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"70bb98ffa892e52b8dd4e8e3269e777533d05187b0fa193d085544ae62c24b39","compact":"b5d8d5e9079b24f95a65a411d902a98672d020671ceaa31e597b74500b1cc0d1","nasal":"c8e2a726d184a8b535af39c10b1a4006eafb35c52b483ed5563623fd7ad6eea5"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-30","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":30,"english":"Her arms were tender like leaves and adorned with various ornaments; truly have the Rākşasas eaten them up, shaken as they were, by throwing them here and there. Alas! did I leave her alone only to be devoured by the Rākşasas? And she has been eaten up like one weak and helpless albeit she has many friends.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.464,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-27","DUTT-3-60-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058030","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3c1375f56e4931e3625cd00c5c822d81952d720dbd7e5e8f2aa3c09f34840ee7","compact":"3e6d460be1becfa5878f1cb55d038ce9d6350e6d5e3eb0db51e03ca8143ff070","nasal":"356e717e9ce8f37db484888cfae69e060dad4a0555f23a0b1cc1e4ee74f4fb41"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-31","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":31,"english":"Alas! did I leave her alone only to be devoured by the Rākşasas? And she has been eaten up like one weak and helpless albeit she has many friends. O Lakşmaņa, O you of mighty-arms, have you seen where my dear wife is? O dear! O Sītā! where have you gone? bewailing again and again in this strain Rāma began to range the forest. Sometimes leaping, sometimes walking in an uncertain direction, again and again he looked like one void of sense.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.42,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-28","DUTT-3-60-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058031","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c39199272ab3a00819f4ab6901741bc847f2ca7ee3fd1a865db4d8a30a5e4f86","compact":"dd54ce920d9e4959805075546ed269bdbe31e7debe1c2da1d7f16c49e04e5a5f","nasal":"803d51145ef42711027dc46393fcf4325739130a0e50711f19d6ac22a9b797e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-32","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":32,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, O you of mighty-arms, have you seen where my dear wife is? O dear! O Sītā! where have you gone? bewailing again and again in this strain Rāma began to range the forest. Sometimes leaping, sometimes walking in an uncertain direction, again and again he looked like one void of sense.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058032","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f862a2257aa245a5fc708b4b0dabfd6af2e87d13eb75e5d10196de1fd9b6e5ee","compact":"406a736eb7b09db57a460269d07b3d17e354ffa63f56896c903114af95a99ee7","nasal":"406a736eb7b09db57a460269d07b3d17e354ffa63f56896c903114af95a99ee7"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-33","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":33,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, O you of mighty-arms, have you seen where my dear wife is? O dear! O Sītā! where have you gone? bewailing again and again in this strain Rāma began to range the forest. Sometimes leaping, sometimes walking in an uncertain direction, again and again he looked like one void of sense. And again intent on searching Sītā he furiously engaged in traversing the rivers, mountains, fountains and the woods. he could not wait patiently anywhere.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.486,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-29","DUTT-3-60-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058033","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ef2ea1218acb2b4acc9d50087320839faadef53578139da43dd6bb255551a200","compact":"c5f470cfe7865d8668f74a72398c2914d8f0a62c0ac3e370a3dcac87f6bf590f","nasal":"5dc4d84ec2d47f705f2900c9bf1c85636967e9f0797d0e4719c7f13e895935cb"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-34","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":34,"english":"And again intent on searching Sītā he furiously engaged in traversing the rivers, mountains, fountains and the woods. he could not wait patiently anywhere.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058034","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"51a0162d9876c1db24ab93be3b94ac53c347b408940cb7cd309e5702e6d00f0a","compact":"591081f17178d49da28d2aed55116429f2dcbeb14966ccd42df173312d537a52","nasal":"591081f17178d49da28d2aed55116429f2dcbeb14966ccd42df173312d537a52"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-58-35","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":58,"verse":35,"english":"Entering a vast forest he searched every nook and corner for Maithilī; his desire was not satisfied and he again engaged with great labour in the finding out of his dear spouse.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.89,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-60-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3058035","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ae4b31d54c547e60303e2a6c2b09c2523b9ec1e405a31d6334d3c9eda4dad4a9","compact":"1745eb253e2f77d245caac56982118374b69c54551d1af26d77dda90b3268996","nasal":"1745eb253e2f77d245caac56982118374b69c54551d1af26d77dda90b3268996"}}]
